cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software and the paper below."
title: "decision-support-rarity: Risk-aware active learning under class rarity"
abstract: >-
  Companion software for the ESWA paper "Risk-aware active learning under class
  rarity: A decision framework and cross-domain evaluation for expert systems".
  It implements a strictly paired-trajectory protocol, an acquisition-risk
  profile (lower quantile and material-loss probability), a non-maximized
  discovery oracle with an exploitability ratio, and evidence-graded guidelines,
  evaluated over 27 acquisition strategies, three downstream learners, a
  synthetic grid, 42 real tabular datasets with preserved rarity, and 17 image
  tasks on two frozen embeddings.
